{
  "about": "Who is using the program (docs/APP-CAPABILITIES-PLAN.md, step 4), as every runtime signs people in. Each case starts from an empty table of people with the rows given (a value {hash, text} is stored as that hash of the text, as clarity-auth's hash makes it), and the sign-in block given. Its steps run in order: signin with a strategy and inputs, which either signs the record of that id in (me) or is refused with a key of Clarity's own words; signout; me, the record signed in now (null for nobody); count, the rows of the table; hashed, text assigned to a hashed field with its minimum (refused, or kept as a hash); save, a person's record saved with new values (a secret changed this way closes the person's other sessions when they changed their own, every session of theirs when someone else did). A served case runs each step as one call of a browser (the step's browser, \"a\" without one) that carries the session cookie the program set it last, from the address given. The tries and sessions of clarity-auth are kept for the whole program, so each case uses names of its own. A case with rememberDays signs in on the desktop as `remember N days` does: a successful sign-in with a strategy that keeps a secret keeps an entry in the program's secret store (the signin block's program, the name clarityRemembered; each runner keeps that store in memory, empty at the case's start); remembered, whether the store holds one; restart, the program starts anew on the same database and secret store (its people named again, nobody signed in) and its start gives the sign-in window, or none (page null) when the remembered sign-in still held and signed its person in. A case with rememberAsks as well signs in as `remember N days when asked` does: the sign-in part asks, and its answer comes as the input remember, \"true\" or \"false\"; only \"true\" keeps the entry. Without rememberAsks the input remember changes nothing.",
  "refusals": {
    "signinRefused": "Signing in did not work. Check what you typed and try again.",
    "signinTooManyTries": "Too many tries. Wait a few minutes and try again.",
    "notAllowed": "You are not allowed to do this.",
    "notYours": "This record is not yours.",
    "secretTooShort": "This needs at least {minimum} characters."
  },
  "people": {
    "table": "members",
    "key": "id",
    "create": "CREATE TABLE members (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, name TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '', email TEXT, login TEXT, password_hash TEXT, api_token TEXT, recovery_codes TEXT)"
  },
  "signin": {
    "page": "SignIn",
    "targets": [
      "desktop",
      "web"
    ],
    "strategies": [
      {
        "name": "password",
        "columns": [
